WEBVTT

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.740
Bishop to g4.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.100
Rook to d4.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.370
That's when we get to f8.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.870
The soldier takes the dragon...

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.120
What are you up to?

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.070
I'm playing chells.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.880
Chells?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.880
I'm recreating a game that I played against 
someone when I was about your age.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.060
You remember that far back?

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.520
I remember every move I've played.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.960
No, I remember everything 
I've seen, heard, or felt.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.990
I don't forget.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.300
Want to play?

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.960
N-No...

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.360
You're a dangerous prisoner.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.280
My brother Najik will get angry 
at me if he knows I talked to you.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.100
I may be from the Dragon Empire,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.040
but I wouldn't eat you like a dragon might.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.930
Hey, what's your name?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.190
Pardon me.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.310
My name is Remedius.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.510
Viscount Remedius Levvi Rahzel.

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.670
Nice to meet you.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.930
What's your name, miss?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.200
I-I'm Naricia.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.320
I don't have a title or family name.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.700
Just Naricia.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.990
<i>Naricia.</i>

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.080
<i>I won't forget your smile, your voice...</i>

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.000
<i>Your everything.</i>

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.470
<b>Bad Omen</b>

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.500
Gayus Levina Soleil.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:38.560
I hereby arrest you on suspicion 
of breaching Jushikiist law.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.300
W-Wait...

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.740
Prepare yourself.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.300
Huh? Hey...

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.610
How?!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.800
How did you do that, Gayus?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.250
H-Hey...

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.970
You aren't getting away now, police lady.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:53.740
Hey...

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.560
Is this fun?

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.260
We may be in love, Jiv, 
but sex lives need variety.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.510
This is kind of pervy.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.760
You say that, but...

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.800
G-Gayus, you idiot.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:09.690
Jiv...

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.270
You should get that.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.490
What are you so cranky about?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.620
I'm always rational.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.060
Even if I'm called to negotiate 
compensation for facilities

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.340
that you destroyed when you went crazy.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.680
Even if that causes our agency, 
which is already in the red,

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.680
to end up even more cash-strapped.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.560
I'm totally fine.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.700
I see.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.760
So that Jivenya woman is
the cause of your frustration.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:49.260
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.740
I'm pissed because you always get 
in the way when I'm making love to her.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.580
Are you asking me to know your mating cycles?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:02.800
Well, better that than someone 
whose fiancée doesn't even care

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.650
if he comes home or not.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.160
<i>Where the hell are you?!</i>

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.410
You assorted bag of useless Jushikiists!

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.480
<i>There's been a sighting of 
abhorrents at Jinorei Firehouse.</i>

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.040
<i>The county police have responded, 
but haven't been able to hold them down.</i>

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.420
<i>Backup from headquarters won't 
make it in time, either.</i>

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.340
<i>That means you're up.</i>

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.760
<i>Get your asses over there.</i>

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.350
<i>Hell, get yourselves killed, 
and you'll make me happy!</i>

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.770
Journalism is serious business!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.590
I don't care if it kills me, 
just let me report on it!

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.270
You take it from here.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.190
Yes, sir.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.760
Is the light gun not here yet?

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.280
Hey, Baylick.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.780
Shit, they already got wind of it.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:53.540
I know the police don't love us, but hi.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.790
So, what's the situation?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.040
A firefighter managed
 to escape and reported to us.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.800
There are still nine people stuck inside.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.920
Premelena was here. A girl with curly red hair.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.430
I feel like you have women everywhere we go.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.010
So, what about the Largonkin Company?

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.940
I'd think they would be the police's 
first choice of private contractors.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:23.820
They left fifteen minutes ago to deal with a 
situation at a dentist's office to the east.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.520
So you asked us, huh?

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.690
I'm grateful.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.200
What's the matter?

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.450
<i>H-Help me...</i>

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.560
Stay calm.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:36.350
What's the situation?

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.120
<i>Th-The enemy is...</i>

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.130
This is awful.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.480
This one's been gassed or poisoned.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:09.240
Not much point working as a low-paid 
cop when you end up dying like this.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.490
Though at least they get 
survivor's pensions, unlike us.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.620
Your blabbermouthedness is terminal.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.180
You're talking, too, 
so that makes you an accomplice.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.870
A Magatsushiki of all things!

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.190
It's a Jushiki interference barrier.

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.300
Amusing.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.730
Gigina, it's a decoy!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.350
There's a Sieru coming!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.360
Above!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.870
Magatsushiki have been called demonic 
and diabolical since ancient times.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.250
Their power is without equal.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.680
Their properties are limitlessly 
evil and devious.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.440
There's a Jushikiist saying:

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.510
"If you're going to fight dragons, 
ancient giants, or Magatsushiki,

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.550
you're better off going home."

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.080
Yeah.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.860
So I want to go home.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.640
Say, Gayus,

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:14.500
couldn't you wait until the plants 
consume the dirt and become bigger?

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:18.570
I'm solving the food security 
crisis for the next century.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.470
If you don't have bread, 
you can always eat dirt.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.710
Now...

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.480
Help me...

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.980
Help me, Gigina!

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.600
Give it up.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.240
You can't be saved.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:03.450
Is... it over?

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:04.830
Hey.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.580
Oh. You.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.090
It's a weak spot that only 
an abhorrent would have.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.120
It couldn't understand

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.720
that we Offensive Jushikiists have 
front line and rear line tactics.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:23.850
It seems you understand 
enough not to drag me down.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.750
They say the protagonist always 
delivers the final blow.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.700
Sucks to be a supporting character, huh?

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.100
We may need to speak through blades.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.230
It's still alive!

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.150
Gayus!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.280
Good grief.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.510
When you fight a Magatsushiki,

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.280
you need to destroy all of its 
brains and hearts, or it won't die.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.900
Isn't that what Diorg taught you?

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.060
I heard you two were in tears,
 and lo and behold...

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:21.030
Is that how Drakens treat people 
who just saved their friends?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.540
Largonkin...

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.870
You ought to learn to mind your manners, too.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.040
I was just making an opportunity for you.

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:32.540
The evening party has already...

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.630
The evening party has already begun?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.800
What is it talking about?

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.550
Three days ago, it was 
the Odal Veterans' Association.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.880
Today, it was here and the dentist's office.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:51.310
All told, there have been four 
Magatsushiki incidents this month.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:56.470
I hope this isn't the beginning of something.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.200
The Tsevellen Dragon Empire 
is a nice place, huh?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.700
I only have bad memories of it.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:13.910
But unlike here in Urmun, no one 
gets killed without reason, do they?

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.990
You won't get killed for talking 
bad about important people

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.690
or for not paying your taxes.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.260
No one dies of hunger.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.790
Women don't get sold off.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:26.820
It sounds like a fairy-tale paradise.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.290
I want to go to the Dragon Empire someday.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:36.280
I'd like to walk beside a river with you.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:52.040
"County police defeat creature conjured 
by illegal Summoning Jushikiists,

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.540
solve Jushikiists murder case."

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:59.610
"Gratitude shown to the city's community safety 
division, who cooperated quickly."

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.050
That asshole Sutherland...

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.770
There you go.

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:10.160
And now it's time for today's happy
 Horton Fortune Telling.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.840
Coffee, please.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.020
Make it really strong.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.280
Oh, Arzel.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.270
You seem pretty tired.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.750
I'm exhausted from working on the 
Magatsushiki case from yesterday.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.790
Want this?

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:22.730
Yes!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.420
If you let me do you once.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:27.500
Seriously?

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.860
I'm kidding.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.760
You have a girlfriend, don't
you? Are you always like this?

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.410
Okay, what if I told you we just broke up?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.580
No way.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:43.550
You're just going to go 
right back to Jivenya again.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.550
Take good care of her.

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:49.800
Yeah.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.050
Here you are.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:58.680
All right.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:00.660
All fueled up.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.440
Are you going to follow up on
the Magatsushiki incident?

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:06.280
Nah, something else this time.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.950
I got news that the Aurora Hammer 
is on the move here in Eridana.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.820
Aurora Hammer?

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.870
They're an anti-government organization 
from the faraway Urmun Republic, aren't they?

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:16.830
Yeah.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.420
We don't know what they're doing in Eridana,

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:25.310
but the head of state, Dochetta, 
is holding a celebration soon.

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:26.720
Is something fishy going on?

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:30.700
Dochetta is originally 
a Numerical Jushikiist.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.770
Apparently, he used to care 
about the nation,

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.300
but he changed completely 
after he won the election.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.100
He's been oppressing his people 
with fear and violence.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:44.120
A typical tyrant, along with the 
poverty and inequality that follows.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:45.610
I wonder what caused it.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.100
Dunno.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:51.080
I'm guessing he gave into despair...

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.750
in the hopeless nation that is Urmun.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.370
In people.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.760
What are you making this time?

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:03.770
A shelf.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.260
Also known as my son.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:08.960
Don't go adding inanimate 
objects to your family.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:11.420
It'll make your inheritance complicated.

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:15.210
We have a client coming soon.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:17.160
Get the details from them.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:17.770
Dude.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.010
I specialize in fighting.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:22.170
You specialize in everything else.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.030
I specialize in cutting.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:26.940
You specialize in receiving pain.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:32.550
Whoosh.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:40.210
You broke it.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.270
I'll break you, too.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.960
How much? One hundred or two hundred?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.280
Hang on!

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:52.320
You bought the materials for 
that chair at the 100 yen shop!

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:54.810
That's worth more than your life!

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.380
Then I'll tell you the truth.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.800
I'm actually Gayus's twin brother, Gayushi.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:07.400
Be that as it may, you're 
the one who broke my chair!

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.910
You just wondered for a second 
if it was true, didn't you?

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.070
Dummy!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.880
Die!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.330
Stop!

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.080
Do you want to get cut down, too?

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.210
Jiv...

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.450
First Cuello, and now her.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.220
You're always hiding behind women.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.160
That was scary...

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.070
Don't put yourself in danger.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.920
This happens all the time.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.440
But he was seriously going to...

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.700
Jiv...

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:01.420
So who's Cuello?

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:05.000
Oh, she's a former fellow Offensive Jushikiist.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.470
She was my woman from way back.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.380
But now...

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.540
You're the only one for me.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:21.890
Come on, you have a guest.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:25.520
I'm going to go to work now.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.770
I got to see you freaking out, too.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:31.580
Just don't get yourself into too much trouble.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.920
I am Egurrd Lasgrissid.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:43.540
I'm an Offensive Jushikiist specializing 
in negotiation and diplomacy.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.950
This here is Calpulnia Levvinakes Rahzel.

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:48.820
The client.

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:53.920
I'm here representing the Rahzel Foundation.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.930
The Rahzel Foundation?

00:17:55.930 --> 00:17:57.050
Of Rahzel Company?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:58.620
Correct.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:01.360
She's the head of Rahzel Company,

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:03.560
one of the few corporate 
giants in the Dragon Empire.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:07.810
What would you ask of a 
private agency like ours?

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:14.480
Do you know of my nephew, 
Remedius Levvi Rahzel?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:15.190
Yes.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:19.150
He's the chells genius who became 
the continental champion

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:21.200
at just eleven years old.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:25.000
Further, he's known to have been the creator

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.760
of almost all of Rahzel Company's 
cutting-edge technology.

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.210
But he...

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:31.440
Yes.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:34.480
On his visit to Urmun Republic two years ago,

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:37.680
he was abducted by an anti-government 
organization known

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:42.140
as the Aurora Hammer, or the Aurora Front, 
as they were known at the time.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.040
He hasn't come home since.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.050
But we've been negotiating under the radar,

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:51.270
and we've finally agreed on a transfer 
of ransom money and the doctor.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:55.670
The transfer is in two days, here in Eridana.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.150
The ransom is two billion yen.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:00.530
Two billion yen?!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.790
And what would you have us do?

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:11.140
We want you to accompany us 
as guards to the exchange point.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:17.040
Egurrd, I don't recall giving you 
permission to smoke next to me.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.800
Pardon me.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:24.050
Our security department lacks Jushikiists 
who are accustomed to violence.

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:28.810
I've heard that you are both 13th-grade.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:31.810
We need you.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:36.570
Of course, we will promise a 
reward fitting of the task.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.700
No smoking in this room.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.050
I won't light it.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:52.460
My wife set a limit for 
the sake of my health.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:56.090
The report on the Jinorei Firehouse.

00:19:56.530 --> 00:20:01.090
Did you make me deliver this just so I'd have
to meet with that loner Largonkin there?

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:06.650
Since Baylick doesn't seem 
to want to say it, I will.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.220
Want to work with us, the Largonkin Company?

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:10.350
What?

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:15.100
First, take a look at this.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.880
These points are where the Magatsushiki

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:22.110
showed up this past month in Eridana.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.680
That <i>is</i> unusually frequent.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:30.370
The mayor personally asked for us 
to recruit private Jushikiists.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:34.360
We at the Largonkin Company 
could deal with it handily ourselves,

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:36.000
but our headquarters is 
on the Alliance side.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:39.800
We're enlisting the help of 
you guys from the Dragon Empire

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.080
so that we can set up a joint front.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:45.280
I wouldn't mind cooperating 
as long as we got paid.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:48.010
But... too bad.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:52.140
We received a request from 
a huge corporation <i>just</i> before yours,

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.200
and we're really busy.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.590
We'll accept <i>any</i> conditions.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:58.900
It's settled.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:02.410
The Largonkin agency will 
mop up the Magatsushiki,

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.900
and Ashley-Bufh & Soleil will assist.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.140
I'm counting on you.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:20.800
It seems our evening party is going well.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:25.960
Your scouts were wiped 
out by the Jushikiists.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.300
Now, it's my men's turn.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:31.240
Please go easy on me.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.980
We'll see if I can.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.030
Now then, the curtains have 
risen on our dazzling spectacle

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:41.990
here in this city of 
conspiracy and deception.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:47.670
It's the beginning of a happy 
play of blood and killing.

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.950
Bloodshed for the sake of bloodshed,

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:56.670
murder for the sake of murder, 
hell for the sake of hell.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.020
Who will make it possible 
to play the first move

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:03.540
and the last move on a 
board of our creation?

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:09.470
You, me, or him...

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.970
Who will have the last laugh?

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:16.180
Let us enjoy it!

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:53.780
Every human is a component.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:58.200
If there was a world that could 
be saved by the might of one alone,

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:03.530
it would be a wretched world 
which would need only that one.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.960
<b>Invitation to an Evening Party</b>
